    "title": "Offer choices or state alternatives",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-alternatives-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Offer choices or state alternatives",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Use 还是 between alternatives in a question, without adding 吗 to that ordinary choice question. Use 或者 to present alternatives in a statement.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "你喝茶还是喝牛奶？",
                "pinyin": "nǐ hē chá háishi hē niúnǎi ？",
                "meaning": "Will you have tea or milk?",
                "audio": "76237bc557af900c0277cf9b798e982736937b81152f34dfa51ec41740235f6a"
              },
              {
                "text": "我喝茶或者喝牛奶。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ hē chá huòzhě hē niúnǎi 。",
                "meaning": "I will have either tea or milk.",
                "audio": "38905baa880b1093acd7efdbcb1b3bad3f3d66d786315c63bf211c64194c27e0"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "还是",
                "pinyin": "háishi",
                "meaning": "or (in alternative questions); had better (preference); still (despite an alternative)",
